From dcc30904b22ba0e0d972ab0fd43a24ecddda8400 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:06:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: touch and mouse, first on the icon rows

One pointer for the desktop build, and later the phone builds
(native/touch.h): the platform reports it (SDL's mouse, which SDL also
feeds from touch; the headless build's new "touch X Y" script command),
and native_touch.c turns it into taps: Touch_TappedRect asks whether a
rectangle was pressed and let go in this frame, Touch_TappedUiRect the
same in the UI safe area's coordinates. Tap targets are at least
TOUCH_TARGET_MIN (24) pixels.

The icon rows take taps (IconMenu_Run, arena_icon_menu.c): tap an icon to
select it, tap it again to choose it. That covers the party manager's
menu and its choice of shop. Keys and the pad work as before.

The GBA ROM is byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ykfbWFo924wEqysLhg
