-Not yet: the window layer (menus, messages, the battle HUD) is still 32
-tiles wide, so at 288 its boxes wrap and the battle command row crashes.
-256 plays through.
+- The window layer (menus, messages, the battle HUD) is 64 tiles wide too:
+  `WINDOW_MAP_WIDTH` and `WINDOW_MAP_ROW_SHIFT` (`window.h`) stand for the
+  32 and the `<< 5` the window code had, and BG0 reads a wide map.
+- The UI's safe area: outside battle the window, screen, menu and shop code
+  (`window.o`, `screens.o`, `menu.o`, `shop.o`, built with
+  `NATIVE_UI_SPACE`) lays out in 240 pixels centred on the screen, so the
+  GBA's screens keep together. `DISPLAY_WIDTH` there is `gNativeUiWidth`;
+  BG0 scrolls by the offset; the sprites that code queues
+  (`Oam_AddSpriteAtDepth`) and the field sprites it places
+  (`Render_ApplyProjectedPlacementFar`) move by it in the OAM builder. In
+  battle the safe area is the whole screen (`Screen_SetUiSafeArea`, called
+  where the window system starts for the field or for battle).
+
+### Touch and mouse
+
+One pointer (`native/touch.h`, `native_touch.c`): the platform reports it
+(`Platform_ReadPointer`: SDL's mouse, which SDL also feeds from touch; the
+headless build's `touch X Y` script command taps at a screen pixel), and game
+code asks `Touch_TappedRect` / `Touch_TappedUiRect` whether a rectangle was
+tapped this frame. Tap targets are at least `TOUCH_TARGET_MIN` (24) pixels.
+So far the icon rows (`IconMenu_Run`: the manager, the shop choice) take taps:
+tap an icon to select it, tap it again to choose it.
 
 The headless build takes the arena repo's smoke scripts (`scripts/smoke/*.txt`:
 `wait`, `press`, `tap`, `mash`, `include`, `shot`, `peek`, `poke`) and writes
